where all compositions with the same domain and ending in 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbb{R}$
\end_inset

 trivially agree.
 The original problem optimizes on 
\begin_inset Formula $\pi(\hat{X})=X$
\end_inset

,
 where 
\begin_inset Formula $S$
\end_inset

 is not convex,
 and correspondingly 
\begin_inset Formula $\hat{S}$
\end_inset

 is not convex on 
\begin_inset Formula $\varepsilon(X)=\hat{X}\cap\{p=1\}$
\end_inset

.
 We will pick a different subset of 
\begin_inset Formula $\hat{X}$
\end_inset

 on which 
\begin_inset Formula $\hat{S}$
\end_inset

 trivially equivalent to a
\emph on
 
\emph default
convex problem.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
To that end,
 we observe that 
\begin_inset Formula $\hat{S}$
\end_inset

 can also be written as 
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{equation}
\hat{S}(z,p)\equiv S(z/p)\equiv\frac{\mu^{\top}z/p-r_{0}}{\sigma(z/p)}\overset{!}{=}\frac{\mu^{\top}z-pr_{0}}{\sigma(z)}.\label{eq:S reformulated}
\end{equation}

\end_inset

 To eliminate the non-convexity here,
 we kill the numerator by picking that slice of 
\begin_inset Formula $\hat{X}$
\end_inset

 where the equality holds:
 
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
X'\coloneqq\hat{X}\cap\left\{ (z,p):\mu^{\top}z-pr_{0}=1\right\} .
\]

\end_inset

To let the abstract nonsense do the job,
 we have to show that 
\begin_inset Formula $X'$
\end_inset

 is punctured uniquely by all rays in 
\begin_inset Formula $\hat{X}$
\end_inset

.
 This is obvious by considering the projection 
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{gather*}
\pi':\hat{X}\to X'\\
\pi'(px,p)\coloneqq(p'_{x}x,p'_{x}),\\
\text{with }p'_{x}\coloneqq1/\left(\mu^{\top}x-r_{0}\right).
\end{gather*}

\end_inset

The choice of the parameter 
\begin_inset Formula $p'_{x}$
\end_inset

 ensures that 
\begin_inset Formula $\pi':\hat{X}\to X'$
\end_inset

 has range 
\begin_inset Formula $X'$
\end_inset

 and is a right inverse of the embedding 
\begin_inset Formula $\varepsilon':X'\hookrightarrow\hat{X}$
\end_inset

,
 
\begin_inset Formula $\varepsilon'(px,p)\coloneqq(px,p).$
\end_inset

 The situation now is illustrated by:
